    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0735" n="1469" xml:id="pg1469"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Knapp, at Bitlis, charged with murder and inciting rebellion. See Dwight for
                    specifications. If practicable, have immediate investigation and report thereon
                    made by Consul Jewitt. If impracticable for Consul Jewitt to immediately act,
                    ask British ambassador to kindly permit British consul, Yan, to investigate and
                    report upon charges.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
